  "comparability_notes": [
    "Cosine is English text similarity, not a percentage of correct semantic translations. Partial structural guesses and tentative wording can obtain nonzero similarity.",
    "Existing 12 Sol scores are reused byte-for-byte with the same pinned embedding revision and package versions; duplicate context-summary entries and the diagnostic checkpoint are excluded.",
    "Task statuses and discarded glyph violations are excluded. Missing/wholly unknown predictions remain zero in the fixed scorable denominator. D05 declares all meanings unknown; D06 explicitly lists unknown; six D11 entries explicitly unknown with structural parentheticals are normalized as abstentions. Raw descriptions are preserved.",
    "All 109 D07 agent entries contain unknown markers and structural/tentative descriptions. Nonzero similarity there does not establish decipherment. Unresolved aliases in other reports are retained.",
    "References are frozen public-only, reference-assisted drafts authored before decoder scoring. Low/medium-confidence entries remain tentative; high-confidence subsets are reported separately. DeepSeek has no high-confidence reference entries.",
    "New decoders use 8 agents, 200 shared turns, no time cap, $50 soft limit. Prior Sol reports mix $40/200-turn and $10/10-minute protocols. Differences do not isolate model or briefing effects.",
    "Haiku and DeepSeek source gameplay did not escape; Gemini and all five Sol sources escaped. This is a descriptive comparison of different source languages/transcripts, not a balanced model leaderboard.",
    "D12 failed during UTF-8 logging and produced no final report. It is unscored, not assigned zero. No new decoder calls are made for this analysis."
  ],
